DroidLabX workbench shell: phone vs tablet layout, strip unused chrome

Phone (<768px): hide the activity rail and explorer behind a titlebar
drawer (hamburger). The editor is the default surface; opening a file
closes the drawer. Tablet/desktop keep the left rail as in stock VS Code.

Product defaults disable Git/SCM, Copilot/chat, command center, accounts,
ports/forwarding, and hide Outline/Timeline. CSS is a fallback for leftover
chrome. Reproduce: open the workbench at 390px vs 1024px; e2e in
test/e2e/droidlabxShell.test.ts.

